{
  "_comment": "Generated by tools/extract/extract_door_poses.py (docs/progress/door-poses.md): the END POSE of every node Arena's gates move, next to the node's closed pose in the scene. barrier = the path of the gate's root (an opened_barriers entry; Equator's booth doors are not barriers: the assembly root under SPAWN_DOORS or Respawn_2), part = the barrier root's direct child (what BoothDoorRepairs switches off; \"\" = the root itself moves), node = the transform path below the part that is animated (\"\" = the part itself), positions and euler angles are LOCAL to the node's parent (Unity localPosition / localEulerAngles). source = clip (a Mecanim clip: Bowl), dotanimator (Arena's DOTween script: Equator, Bay5) or borrowed (Arena authors no motion for this gate; a neighbour's is used). seconds = Arena's own duration, unscaled. ease = smoothstep (the client's stand-in for Bowl's clips), linear, inOutQuint or curve (curve = Hermite keys [time, value, inSlope, outSlope] on a 0..1 timeline). at = null, or the WORLD position of the barrier root instance (tells repeated hierarchy paths apart, matched within 0.05 m). Euler angles of clip poses are the clip's own raw values (interpolate component-wise); rotations of dotanimator poses are interpolated as a quaternion slerp between the two triples. ArenaMapRegistry.<Map>.DoorPoses mirrors this file number for number (validate_map_descriptors.py and the DoorPoseSidecarTests). Object names and derived numbers only (the curve keys are derived numbers too); no Arena asset or file is stored. A row with a \"switch\" key {closed, open} switches the node on or off instead of moving it (AirPit's passport lamps: closed = the node's active state in the scene, open = the state Arena's DotAnimator sets; the row's transforms are the node's scene transform on both sides, seconds is Arena's duration word, 0 for a switch). A part name may repeat among a barrier's direct children (the 16 passport leaves reuse 6 names): such rows are told apart by their closed position, matched within 0.05 m. A borrowed row whose clip says \"static open pose\" takes the open pose from a neighbour that stands open in the scene (AirPit's bus doors); its seconds are the port's, not Arena's.",
